column-is-layout-flow"><div style="height:31px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div><h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont has-theme-secondary-color has-text-color"><strong>More About Playing Preschool Year 1</strong></h2><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Playing Preschool Year 1 is a 314-page PDF.</strong> You will receive immediate access and an email with a link to your online profile with lifetime access to your purchase.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Playing Preschool was carefully designed to support parents because the early years should be joyful, not stressful.</strong> <em>In addition to the daily lesson plans, you will also receive:</em></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>A <strong>Start-Up Guide</strong> to help you teach with confidence from the very first lesson</li><li>A <strong>full book list</strong> for each of the 19 thematic units</li><li><strong>Detailed supply lists</strong> for every unit</li><li>More than 350 <strong>hands-on activities</strong></li><li>Nineteen<strong> unit poems and songs</strong> to build phonemic awareness</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>This program is sold as a non-refundable digital PDF.</strong></p></div><div class="wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div style="height:31px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div><div class="wp-block-image starsrightbottom"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1553" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1.jpg" alt="Playing Preschool homeschool curriculum spiral-bound book with a blue cover, lying on a white surface surrounded by crayons, scissors, glue, pom-poms, and colorful paper. The cover shows a child's hands nestled in a pile of colorful pom-poms." class="wp-image-174258" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1.jpg 1200w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-232x300.jpg 232w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-791x1024.jpg 791w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-768x994.jpg 768w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-1187x1536.jpg 1187w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-640x828.jpg 640w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-500x647.jpg 500w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-655x848.jpg 655w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%201200%201553%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="1200" height="1553" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1.jpg" alt="Playing Preschool homeschool curriculum spiral-bound book with a blue cover, lying on a white surface surrounded by crayons, scissors, glue, pom-poms, and colorful paper. The cover shows a child's hands nestled in a pile of colorful pom-poms." class="lazyload wp-image-174258" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1.jpg 1200w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-232x300.jpg 232w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-791x1024.jpg 791w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-768x994.jpg 768w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-1187x1536.jpg 1187w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-640x828.jpg 640w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-500x647.jpg 500w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Playing-Preschool-1-655x848.jpg 655w" data-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure></div></div></div></div></div></div><div style="height:40px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div><h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-button-color-color has-text-color has-link-color wp-elements-1"><strong>Discover the Magic of Playing Preschool </strong></h2><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>You are your child&#8217;s best teacher, </strong>and with the Playing Preschool program, you&#8217;ll have everything you need to make that happen.</p><div class="wp-block-columns infoblocks is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-style-shape1 is-style-bgstyle1 is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="220" height="220" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon.png" alt="ABC blocks icon" class="wp-image-174251" style="aspect-ratio:1.3333333333333333;object-fit:contain;width:auto;height:80px" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon-125x125.png 125w" sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20220%20220%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="220" height="220" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon.png" alt="ABC blocks icon" class="lazyload wp-image-174251" style="aspect-ratio:1.3333333333333333;object-fit:contain;width:auto;height:80px" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Blocks-icon-125x125.png 125w" data-sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></figure></div><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont margin10" style="font-size:21px">Play-Based</h3><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">Meaningful learning through play, not worksheets or drills. Every activity is designed to teach through hands-on discovery, not pages to fill out.</p></div><div class="wp-block-column is-style-shape2 is-style-bgstyle2 color-bluetwo is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="220" height="220" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon.png" alt="magnifying glass icon" class="wp-image-174252" style="width:auto;height:80px" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon-125x125.png 125w" sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20220%20220%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="220" height="220" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon.png" alt="magnifying glass icon" class="lazyload wp-image-174252" style="width:auto;height:80px" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Magnifying-Glass-Icon-125x125.png 125w" data-sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></figure></div><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont margin10" style="font-size:21px">Intentional</h3><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">Every lesson is designed for you and your child to do together, turning ordinary days into lifelong memories you&#8217;ll both treasure.</p></div><div class="wp-block-column is-style-shape3 is-style-bgstyle3 color-greentwo is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="220" height="220" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon.png" alt="crayons icon" class="wp-image-174253" style="width:auto;height:80px" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon-125x125.png 125w" sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20220%20220%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="220" height="220" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon.png" alt="crayons icon" class="lazyload wp-image-174253" style="width:auto;height:80px" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Crayons-Icon-125x125.png 125w" data-sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></figure></div><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont margin10" style="font-size:21px">Low-Prep</h3><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">Materials and instructions are laid out for you, lesson by lesson. Open the program, gather from the unit supply lists, and start teaching.</p></div></div><div class="wp-block-columns infoblocks is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-style-shape1 is-style-bgstyle1 color-greentwo is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="220" height="220" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon.png" alt="calendar icon" class="wp-image-174254" style="width:auto;height:80px" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon-125x125.png 125w" sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20220%20220%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="220" height="220" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon.png" alt="calendar icon" class="lazyload wp-image-174254" style="width:auto;height:80px" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Calendar-icon-125x125.png 125w" data-sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></figure></div><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont margin10" style="font-size:21px">Structured</h3><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">A clear, planned rhythm for every single day. You&#8217;ll always know what&#8217;s next, without having to build it yourself or fill in blanks.</p></div><div class="wp-block-column is-style-shape2 is-style-bgstyle2 color-yellowtwo is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="220" height="220" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon.png" alt="puzzle icon" class="wp-image-174255" style="width:auto;height:80px" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon-125x125.png 125w" sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20220%20220%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="220" height="220" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon.png" alt="puzzle icon" class="lazyload wp-image-174255" style="width:auto;height:80px" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Puzzle-Icon-125x125.png 125w" data-sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></figure></div><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont margin10" style="font-size:21px">Open-Ended</h3><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">Playing Preschool meets your child where they are, with room to grow and explore at their own pace. The program flexes and adapts to the child.</p></div><div class="wp-block-column is-style-shape3 is-style-bgstyle3 is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><noscript><img decoding="async" width="220" height="220" src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon.png" alt="House icon" class="wp-image-174256" style="width:auto;height:80px" srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon-125x125.png 125w" sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20220%20220%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" width="220" height="220" data-src="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon.png" alt="House icon" class="lazyload wp-image-174256" style="width:auto;height:80px" data-srcset="https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon.png 220w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon-180x180.png 180w, https://shop.busytoddler.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/PP-House-Icon-125x125.png 125w" data-sizes="(max-width: 220px) 100vw, 220px" /></figure></div><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont margin10" style="font-size:21px">Affordable</h3><p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">Priced with real families in mind. This is engaging early learning without the financial strain of preschool tuition or expensive materials.</p></div></div><hr class="wp-block-separator has-text-color has-button-color-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-button-color-background-color has-background is-style-dots"/><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-container alignfull is-style-redborder gb-block-container" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding-bottom:1%;padding-top:1%"><div class="gb-container-inside"><div class="gb-container-content" style="max-width:1100px"><div class="wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center margin0 is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div style="height:27px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div><h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center is-style-parafont has-button-color-color has-text-color"><strong>Frequently Asked Questions</strong></h2><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-container gb-block-container"><div class="gb-container-inside"><div class="gb-container-content" style="max-width:760px"><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>Is Playing Preschool a book or an ebook? Can I get a hard copy?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Playing Preschool is an ebook. </strong>The PDFs will be delivered to your email address immediately after checkout. They will also be listed at the bottom of your receipt.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The downloads for Playing Preschool do not expire.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>I do not sell a hard copy. </strong>It&#8217;s more cost-effective to sell the program as a digital download, and it also allows me to offer the program worldwide. The program can be used digitally or printed. <em>You are permitted to print one copy of Playing Preschool for your use.</em></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>For online print shops, check out:</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><a href="https://www.watsonfamilypress.com">Watson Family Press</a> (code: BUSY10 for 10% off*)</li><li><a href="http://www.Thehomeschoolprintingcompany.com">The Homeschool Printing Company</a></li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Print in black and white, lightest weight paper, and double-sided. I also have mine spiral-bound on the long edge.</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">*Not an affiliate code, just a very generous offer from a small business.</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>What is the age range for Playing Preschool?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The age range is broad: from 2.5 to 5 years old.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here&#8217;s why: this is an open-ended program. It meets children where they are developmentally by asking open-ended questions and using open-ended activities. Children of varying ages can be asked the same questions, but answers will differ based on their developmental level. <em>Unlike workbooks and computer programs, Playing Preschool works across a wide range of developmental levels thanks to this technique.</em></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">For example, a three-year-old and a five-year-old will answer the question <em>“Why do you think an apple is round?”</em> in vastly different, but valid ways. An open-ended program, like Playing Preschool, allows for variations and child-led learning as opposed to fill-in-the-blank or multiple-choice learning.</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>My child is 4, and knows their letters. Can I skip Year 1?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>I always recommend starting with Year 1, no matter what.</strong> I was a kindergarten teacher, and I wrote Year 1 from that lens.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">I started by determining my “wish list” skills that kids would enter kindergarten with, and that list ended up full of thinking skills, rather than memorized skills like the ABCs or counting. I built a program that goes beyond memorized learning and into these so-called “thinking skills&#8221; as well as exposing kids to a breadth of background experiences and knowledge that are critical.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Playing Preschool Year 1 is filled with skills for kids that span multiple subject areas, such as sorting (used in reading, math, and science). I never dreamed I’d write a Year 2 (that just happened). <strong>My goal was Year 1 as a way to set kids up for success into Kindergarten.</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>I also wrote Year 1 when my oldest was 4+.</em> At that time, he knew all his letters and numbers, and could read numbers to 1000. He was well into addition and even beginning to toy with repeated addition, aka multiplication. But I wrote this program to take him deeper into his learning and help him develop richer skills, because I knew, as a teacher, that memorizing facts is actually a really low-level, basic skill. Sure, it’s fun that he could memorize quickly, but I wanted to see him doing more with his learning.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">During Year 1, Playing Preschool focuses on sorting and classifying data, reading a graph, conceptual understanding of numerals, addition and subtraction, understanding the various uses of numbers beyond counting, recalling key details, retelling information in sequence, non-standard forms of measurement, predicting, and understanding cause and effect. Year 2 expands on the work a child did in Year 1. Without it, Year 2 can feel bulky and clunky.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">The open-ended activities (many of which I pulled straight from my kindergarten and first grade classrooms) allow kids to explore, create, imagine, evaluate, and build their knowledge with their hands. I also added extensions into the program as simple ways to “up the challenge” for children who are ready for that.</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>Can I start before age 2.5?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>I set the earliest starting age at 2.5 years old for several developmental reasons.</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">At 2.5, there are often some big gains in communication and motor skills. For the program to be a success, the child needs at least a 5-10-minute attention span, the ability to ask and answer questions thoughtfully, and the ability to start a task and see it through to completion. They also need their own life experience and background knowledge in place to make sense of the new information being shared. Playing Preschool also requires a lot of fine motor skills needed to make the activities work.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">When we think about a child and age differences, consider the impact six months can have, from 18 months to 2 years old. That same kind of giant leap happens between 2 and 2.5.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Alternatively, remember that 2.5 is the <em>earliest</em> I recommend starting, but that doesn’t mean 2.5 is the right starting place for all kids. When I wrote the program, my daughter was 2.5 years old. She did great. She had a ball. Years later, my youngest was nowhere close to ready at 2.5 years old. I waited to start until closer to 4 years old with him because earlier doesn’t mean better with kids – look at each child individually to find their right path.</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>How do I print Playing Preschool?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph">I strongly suggest looking at online options for printing the program, rather than a chain copying center (which I’ve seen quotes as high as $160!). If you do have to use a big box store, make sure to follow my suggestions (below) and do a quick Google search for a promo code.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can also check with your local library, as many have inexpensive printing options. Your files do not need to be printed at once. You can print unit-by-unit.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>For online print shops, check out:</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><a href="https://www.watsonfamilypress.com">Watson Family Press</a> (use code BUSY10 for 10% off)*</li><li><a href="http://www.Thehomeschoolprintingcompany.com">The Homeschool Printing Company</a></li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Print in black and white, lightest weight paper, and double-sided. I also have mine spiral-bound on the long edge.</strong></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">*Not an affiliate code, just a very generous offer from a small business</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>Is Playing Preschool religion-based?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph">No, Playing Preschool is a secular homeschool program. It doesn&#8217;t align with any religion, but is flexible and can be adapted to your family&#8217;s values.</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>Are there lots of supplies needed for Playing Preschool?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph">No. There is a master supply list for the whole year in the Start-Up guide that you&#8217;ll want to make sure to have on hand. There are also a few unit-specific extras needed (like seeds for the plant unit or a stuffed animal for the teddy bear unit). Each unit plan includes a two-week supply list comprised of supplies from the master list and those few unit-specific items.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">What&#8217;s on that master list? It&#8217;s stuff you probably already have, like sticky notes, playing cards, washable paint, and construction paper. <em>It&#8217;s &#8220;Busy Toddler&#8221; style supplies. </em></p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">I built Playing Preschool this way on purpose. You shouldn&#8217;t need a shopping spree to teach your preschooler at home. Most of what you&#8217;ll need is probably already in your home.</p></div></details></div><div class="wp-block-genesis-blocks-gb-accordion gb-block-accordion"><details><summary class="gb-accordion-title"><strong>Do I need to start Playing Preschool in the fall?</strong></summary><div class="gb-accordion-text"><p class="wp-block-paragraph">No, Playing Preschool is not a calendar-based program. It is considered &#8220;evergreen,&#8221; meaning you can start, stop, take breaks, and work through the program at your own pace without worrying about seasons or holidays.</p></div></details></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><hr class="wp-block-separator has-text-color has-button-color-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-button-color-background-color has-background is-style-dots"/><div style='display:none;' class='shareaholic-canvas' data-app='share_buttons' data-title='Playing Preschool Year 1' data-link='https://shop.busytoddler.com/product/playing-preschool-complete-program/' data-summary='Preschool is so much more than memorizing the ABCs and 123s. Playing Preschool Year 1 is a comprehensive, secular, play-based program designed to build a strong educational foundation while honoring how young children learn best. Across 19 thoughtfully sequenced units, children build skills in literacy, math, science, art, and motor development through carefully selected read-alouds, curated discussions, and hands-on activities. Children investigate ideas, make connections, and share their' data-app-id-name='post_below_content'></div></div></div><section class="related products"><h2>Related products</h2><ul class="products columns-4"><li class="entry product type-product post-11858 status-publish first instock product_cat-ebook has-post-thumbnail downloadable virtual taxable purchasable product-type-simple"> <a href="https://shop.busytoddler.com/product/playing-preschool-year-2/" class="woocommerce-LoopProduct-link woocommerce